From bbd98ebee769a510ff7ab134758eb2ce9236823c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:24:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] One tap: Orre Colosseum

A Format selector joins the launcher -- Free, the default, changes nothing at
all; Orre Colosseum makes the whole ruleset happen with no further clicks.

In-game rules, pinned. Instead of guessing at clause bytes whose meanings are
not all mapped, the preset writes the game's OWN stock LV100 tournament
ruleset -- all 144 bytes, read from a clean main.dol -- into the Custom 1
slot, changing exactly one value: entries becomes 4, for bring-6-pick-4. The
menu globals pin to Double / Custom 1, and since the rules screen renders from
those globals, it shows the truth. The venue stays on the field-proven record
pin; the do-not-pin findings (the getter's rebuilt working buffer, the venue
context field that races a random roll) are honored.

Clauses the game cannot enforce, enforced where teams travel. Submissions --
pastes and save bundles alike -- and the host's own two parties are validated:
Gen 1-3 only, restricted legendaries and mythicals refused by name, no
duplicate items, no duplicate species, no Soul Dew. Guests get the reason in
room chat; a non-compliant host is blocked from opening the room at all; and
anyone pasting a non-compliant team with the format on is told at paste time,
long before any gate. Sleep, Freeze and Self-KO remain what they have always
been -- honor rules -- and the UI says so rather than pretending.

Rooms announce the format: hosted session names carry an [Orre] prefix.

And the bundled default teams are now format-legal themselves: all six
template mons held Leftovers, so a fresh install with the format on would have
been refused by its own gate before hosting a single room -- the audit's
sharpest catch. Each template mon now holds a distinct item, rewritten through
the fork's own save library and validated by the fork's own rules code.

Version 1.4.0.
